# [K64] REGRESSION — G2 ([OPT-PRECHECK-ADMIT]) MAY DECLINE THE NECESSARY-BYTE
# PRE-CHECK ON THE VM ROUTE ONLY WHERE THE ONE ATTEMPT IS LINEAR
# (docs/dev/known_issues.md K64; docs/spec/tuning.md §2.29; the reading is
# docs/dev/optloop/cycle2_admitfix_reading.md §1).
#
# Block 1 is `email-nested-plus`'s pattern under `--engine=vm`: a FRAMED
# (`RX_VM_FRAMELESS 0`), unguarded (`RX_VM_PREFILTER "none"`), `^`-anchored
# program. Its one attempt over a leading class run of length L costs
# `3·2^(L-2) - 2` steps before failing on the absent `@`, so at 6ef76820 (G2
# declining on `Job.start_anchor` alone) every `n` cell below GAVE UP
# (`steps`, driver exit 3, a hard failure) where PCRE2 answers NOMATCH; with
# the pre-check emitted the call returns NOMATCH after one `memchr` and no
# VM step. The bench's five subjects (`sd-empty-alt-*`, `sec-github-pat`,
# `v-uuid-*`, L = 36..93) do the same under the DEFAULT budget; the block
# uses `budget steps=10000` and runs of L = 16..20 instead so that the
# failing direction costs milliseconds and python `re` (which has no such
# check and backtracks the same way) can still verify every `n` here.
#
# The `gu` cell is the CONTROL that the budget really reaches the VM: with
# the `@` present no pre-check can help, and the same run still exhausts the
# block's budget — at both pins, as PCRE2 does past its own match limit. It
# proves the `n` cells pass because of the pre-check, not because 10000
# steps happened to be enough.
#
# Block 2 is the frameless arm G2 still declines on: a program that never
# pushes a resume frame cannot backtrack, so its one attempt is linear and
# the same subjects answer NOMATCH inside the same budget with no pre-check.
# (tests/codegen/run_prechecks.sh §5.5 asserts the two stamps; this file
# asserts the answers.)

pattern ^([a-zA-Z0-9._%+-]+)+@
engine vm
budget steps=10000
n "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa"
n "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa"
n "a1b2c3d4-e5f6.7_8%9+"
n "ghp_0123456789abcdef"
m "abc@x" 0 4
gu steps "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa!@"

pattern ^[a-zA-Z0-9._%+-]+@
engine vm
budget steps=10000
n "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa"
n "a1b2c3d4-e5f6.7_8%9+"
m "abc@x" 0 4
